ia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","c":3},{"y":1675,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1675: the French occupation of Trier ends.","cp":"kingdom-of-france","cpn":"Kingdom of France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","c":3},{"y":1690,"t":"capital_move","x":"1690: the archbishop-electors take up residence at Koblenz.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koblenz","c":2},{"y":1705,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1705: the French stay in Trier, to 1714.","cp":"kingdom-of-france","cpn":"Kingdom of France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","c":3},{"y":1714,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1714: the French occupation of Trier ends.","cp":"kingdom-of-france","cpn":"Kingdom of France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","c":3},{"y":1735,"t":"occupation_start","x":"1735: French troops occupy Trier again, until 1737.","cp":"kingdom-of-france","cpn":"Kingdom of France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","c":3},{"y":1737,"t":"occupation_end","x":"1737: the French leave Trier ('the French, who stayed until 1737').","cp":"kingdom-of-france","cpn":"Kingdom of France","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","c":3},{"y":1794,"t":"occupation_start","x":"August 1794: French Republican troops take Trier.","m":8,"cp":"french-first-republic","cpn":"French First Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","c":2},{"y":1801,"t":"occupation_end","x":"9 February 1801: the Treaty of Lunéville ends the occupation by annexation.","m":2,"cp":"french-first-republic","cpn":"French First Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_mediatisation","c":3},{"y":1801,"t":"loss","x":"1801: the left bank of the Rhine passes to France.","m":2,"cp":"french-first-republic","cpn":"French First Republic","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_mediatisation","c":3},{"y":1803,"t":"loss","x":"25 February 1803: the Final Recess gives the right bank to Nassau.","m":2,"cp":"nassau-weilburg","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_mediatisation","c":3},{"y":1803,"t":"dissolve","x":"1803: the Electorate of Trier ends.","m":2,"u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_mediatisation","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Four Lords' War","from":1324,"to":1326,"outcome":"The Baldwin of Luxembourg page says only that he 'took part in the Four Lords' War against Metz, 1324-1326'; it gives no territorial result.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baldwin_of_Luxembourg"},{"name":"Boppard War","from":1497,"to":1497,"outcome":"The townsfolk turned to Maximilian I in 1496; the war of 1497 ended with Boppard acknowledging the Elector as its ruler.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boppard"},{"name":"Thirty Years' War (Trier episodes)","from":1630,"to":1637,"outcome":"Trier opened its gates to Spanish troops in 1630, was captured by the French in 1632 and retaken by Spain in 1635, which imprisoned the Elector Sötern; Imperial troops dispelled the French garrison of Ehrenbreitstein in 1637.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier"},{"name":"French occupations of Trier, 1673-1737","from":1673,"to":1737,"outcome":"French armies occupied Trier 1673-1675, 1684, 1688, 1702, 1705-1714 and 1735-1737, destroying walls, fortresses and many towns of the electorate in 1684-1689; no land changed hands.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier"},{"name":"French Revolutionary Wars (left bank of the Rhine)","from":1794,"to":1801,"outcome":"French troops took Trier in August 1794 and occupied the left bank from 1795; the Treaty of Lunéville (9 February 1801) conceded the left bank to France.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_mediatisation"}],"certainty":[{"from":898,"to":1794,"level":"soft","note":"The electorate was a patchwork of lordships, pledges and exclaves along the Moselle; no survey or treaty line is dated on the pages opened."},{"from":1795,"to":1803,"level":"sharp","note":"The Rhine as the line of the French annexation (Lunéville, 9 February 1801); the right bank remnant is still soft."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electorate_of_Trier","title":"Electorate of Trier"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baldwin_of_Luxembourg","title":"Baldwin of Luxembourg"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pr%C3%BCm_Abbey","title":"Prüm Abbey"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boppard","title":"Boppard"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/German_mediatisation","title":"German mediatisation"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koblenz","title":"Koblenz"}]}